#%PAM-1.0
# Backs vsftpd's virtual-user login (see vsftpd.conf's pam_service_name
# and Containerfile.vsftpd's own comment for the two real, strace-
# confirmed gotchas in wiring this up at all: the GDBM-not-Berkeley-DB
# format, and db= being used as an exact, unsuffixed path) — checks
# against the small GDBM file built into the image, not /etc/shadow.
# crypt=none is a third one: pam_userdb.so otherwise assumes the
# database's stored value is itself a crypt() hash and compares against
# that, which fails with no other diagnostic available in this minimal
# container when the database holds a plain password, as built here.
auth    required    pam_userdb.so   db=/etc/vsftpd/virtual_users crypt=none
account required    pam_userdb.so   db=/etc/vsftpd/virtual_users crypt=none
